            <ArticleTitle>Primary pancreatic lymphoma presenting as acute pancreatitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>403-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary pancreatic lymphoma is a rare disease and usually presents with nonspecific symptoms like abdominal pain, weight loss, or jaundice. Here we report a case of primary pancreatic lymphoma presenting as acute pancreatitis.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2003 S. Karger AG, Basel and IAP</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
